	(text "FEEDBACK DIVIDER (ETA8156, VFB = 0.600V)\n\nVout = VFB x (1 + Rtop / Rbot)\nRbot = R2 = 15k (FB to GND, always in circuit)\nRtop = the series leg selected by the bridged solder jumper (VBUCK to FB)\n\nVout   Rtop (series)       Rtop    Vout calc                 Jumper\n1.20V  15k                 15k     0.6 x (1 + 15/15)  = 1.200V   JP1\n1.80V  15k + 15k           30k     0.6 x (1 + 30/15)  = 1.800V   JP2\n2.50V  47k                 47k     0.6 x (1 + 47/15)  = 2.480V   JP3\n3.30V  47k + 10k + 10k     67k     0.6 x (1 + 67/15)  = 3.280V   JP4\n5.00V  100k + 10k          110k    0.6 x (1 + 110/15) = 5.000V   JP5\n\nBridge exactly ONE jumper. With none bridged, FB sits at 0V and the\noutput is driven toward VIN. With two bridged, the legs are in parallel\nand Vout is wrong. JP4 ships bridged.\nValues are E24 0402 JLCPCB basic parts. Tolerance 1%: Vout is about +/-1.5%.\nThe 6A load drops about 60mV across the 10mOhm shunt, because FB senses before it."
		(at 18.288 176.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Courier New")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c1a557fb-7b47-4d40-848e-71841d1d015a")
	)
